invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_from_bytes takes word i from the eight bytes that start
  8 * i bytes from the front, where the number's least significant word is
  its last eight bytes. A number of 16 bytes or more then has its words in
  the reverse order, and one whose length is no multiple of 8 also loses
  bytes. bin/rsa_equiv_test holds the byte moves to a loop of one byte at
  a time at every length.

--- old
        words[i] = word_from_bytes(bytes + len - 8 * (i + 1));
--- new
        words[i] = word_from_bytes(bytes + 8 * i);
